    "title": "Road racing: Sanders, Sullivan top finishers in Battle of Stonington 5K | Latest Sports | thewesterlysun.com",
    "text": "STONINGTON — William Sanders and Elizabeth Sullivan were the top finishers in the Battle of Stonington 5K in Stonington Borough on Tuesday.\nSanders, 38, of Marlborough, Conn., won the 3.1-mile race — two laps around the borough — in 15:51. Sullivan, 24, of Portsmouth, was the top female in 16:53, which was good for second overall.\nRounding out the Top 10 finishers were Mitchell Jacob of Mystic (third overall, 17:04), Lucas Heide of Ledyard, Conn. (fourth, 17:24), Andrew Brown of New London, Conn. (fifth, 17:26), Greyson Stephenson of Ledyard, Conn. (sixth, 17:27), Raymond Grogan of Gales Ferry, Conn. (seventh, 17:49), Mitchell Tamul of Norwich, Conn. (eighth, 18:26), Alexander Olendorf of Mystic (ninth, 18:07) and Connor Delaney of Mystic (10th, 18:27).\nTop 10 female finishers behind Sullivan were Molly Musselman of Pawcatuck (2nd female, 16th overall, 21:38), Joan Kaijala of Cumberland Center, Me. (3rd, 23rd, 19:35), Linda Spooner of Sturbridge, Mass. (4th, 29th, 20:02), Emily Stefanski of West Kingston (5th, 31st, 20:26), Maggie Littler of Ledyard, Conn. (6th, 33rd, 20:29), Shelly Rivera of Mystic, Conn. (7th, 36th, 20:38), Mackenzie Spooner of Durham, Conn. (8th, 41st, 20:52), Hannah Gigliotti of Waterford, Conn. (9th, 21:01) and Kate Johnston of Bradford (10th, 21:06).\nThere were 314 finishers.\nThe race benefits programming and operations at Stonington Free Library.\n— Rich Zalusky",
